.TH alloc_zero 3
.SH NAME
alloc_zero \- allocate and zero-initialize memory
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <alloc.h>

void* alloc_zero(size_t \fIn\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alloc_zero
allocates \fIn\fP bytes of memory using
.BR alloc (3)
and initializes the entire block to zero using
.BR byte_zero (3).

If the allocation fails, it returns NULL.
.SH SEE ALSO
alloc(3), alloc_re(3), byte_zero(3)